# Intent: Reversi (spec docs/design/reversi.md, rank 3 of docs/plan/more-games.md): 8 by 8, the person plays black and moves first, the unit plays white with a two-ply search over a positional table (at most a few hundred nodes a move, bounded by a host test); passes are automatic; the game ends when neither side can move and shows You won, You lost or Draw with the disc count. Two new header-only files: the pure core and the screen (the board is ONE object with one draw callback, cells of 25 px). Registering the game, the touches (rv_hit), the unit's move after a short pause, the sounds, the best score and the game-over call are the firmware track's.
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/maipai_reversi_core.h, maipai_reversi.h (new, ours)
# Check after a flash: Games, Reversi: the board with four discs and amber dots on the four legal cells; a tap on a dotted cell flips discs and the unit answers within a moment; a side with no move passes with a line saying so; the end shows the shared game-over screen with the disc count.
# Kconfig: none

